         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus with the chain rule, the derivative is the integrand evaluated at the upper limit times the derivative of the upper limit: \\( h^{\\prime}(x) = \\left(x^{6} + 2\\right) \\cdot 3 x^{2} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99024",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus with a composite upper limit"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At x = -2 the upper limit is -8, the integrand at \\( t = -8 \\) is \\( 66 \\), and the derivative of the upper limit is 12, so \\( h^{\\prime}(-2) = 66 \\cdot 12 = 792 \\).",
